  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read status",
      "items": [
        "IMPLEMENTED = code exists in the pinned repository/commit; SERVING adds that the path runs on the live tutor/CLA request path",
        "sources[] = file:line verified at syllabai-core @ 14b5e3d via Archify evidence verification",
        "NOT SERVED / UNWIRED / no-op v0 / degrades are explicit statuses — never read them as live capability"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What is NOT serving today",
      "items": [
        "Lexical BM25 arm — implemented against the V28 column, but enters the served fusion only if the T-C13 benchmark promotes it",
        "RetrievalFabric multi-arm orchestrator — deliberately not a Spring bean, zero consumers by design (explicit composition, run-003-b E-1)",
        "Gemini File Search arm — stub with available() = false",
        "Vector leg degrades honestly to empty (KG-only evidence) when no embedding provider is keyed; ingestion paused pending Embedding v2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Truth boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The authoritative KG is canonical curriculum truth — retrieval-derived graph signals (Local Intelligence Layer) are PROPOSED and appear nowhere in serving",
        "Serving retrieval is NOT PDF→chunks→embeddings→vector DB→LLM: it is curriculum-scope-gated hybrid retrieval (KG + vector) fused rank-only, capped, and refused deterministically when nothing survives",
        "LLMs generate from the assembled context only — they never mark answers and never own curriculum truth",
        "Every citation resolves from surviving evidence items; there is no free-floating claim path. The sufficiency→generator edge is intentionally unlabeled: admission-on-pass is the gate's contract, refusal is documented here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Sources",
      "items": [
        "All 12 nodes are syllabai-core packages, pinned at 14b5e3d780956b39267bce2a8b831865ca4f89bb",
        "KaRAG pipeline contract (intent → KG context → hybrid retrieval → fusion → rerank → grounded generation → citations) is documented in KaRagService.java:18-19",
        "CLA follows the same contract (ClaService.java:59-61) with the §7 answer-leakage gate (ClaLeakagePolicy)"
      ]
    }
